@798400 Please backup your files, connect the drive to a PC and follow these steps:

A. Click Start;
B. Right click on "Computer" or "My Computer";
C. Select "Manage";
D. Click on "Disk Management";
(On Windows 10, go to the Control Panel and click Administrative Tools and then Computer

@798400 Management. Click Disk Management).
E. Select the Seagate hard drive;
F. Right-click on the large box on the right and select "Delete Volume" or "Delete Partition";
G. Right-click in the part that says "unallocated";
H. Select "New Simple Volume or New Partition";

